<title>NETHERLANDS: Universal says cuts runs at its Antwerp refinery.</title>
<headline>Universal says cuts runs at its Antwerp refinery.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Universal said on Tuesday it cut runs at its 60,000 barrel per day (bpd) refinery in Antwerp by 15 percent because of poor margins.</p>
<p>&quot;Since yesterday, we reduced runs by 15 percent as the margins were terrible,&quot; a company source said.</p>
<p>The cut reduced capacity to 50,000 bpd, the source said.</p>
<p>The Universal refinery is 100 percent owned by Daewoo Corp of South Korea.</p>
